      "description": "Grouped unit controls with visible selection.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-units\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Units\"><button aria-pressed=\"true\" aria-label=\"Use metric units\">°C</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\" aria-label=\"Use imperial units\">°F</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-units{display:inline-flex;padding:3px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e5e5df);border-radius:8px;background:var(--ground,#f6f5f1)}.ds-units button{font-family:\"DM Sans\",system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:38px;height:36px;border:0;border-radius:5px;background:transparent;color:var(--muted,#696b64);cursor:pointer}.ds-units button[aria-pressed=\"true\"]{background:var(--surface,#fff);color:var(--text,#292b28)}.ds-units button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#9d4224);outline-offset:4px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "City search field",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "input-search",
      "description": "Grounded search field focused as a whole form.",
      "html": "<form class=\"ds-field\" role=\"search\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"11\" r=\"8\"/><path d=\"m21 21-4.3-4.3\"/></svg><input aria-label=\"Search for a city\" placeholder=\"Find a city…\"/><button type=\"button\">Search</button></form>",
      "css": ".ds-field{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;height:44px;max-width:528px;padding-left:14px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e5e5df);border-radius:8px;background:var(--ground,#f6f5f1)}.ds-field:focus-within{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#9d4224);outline-offset:2px}.ds-field svg{width:18px;height:18px;fill:none;stroke:var(--muted,#696b64);stroke-width:1.65;stroke-linecap:round}.ds-field input{font-family:\"DM Sans\",system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;min-width:0;width:100%;height:100%;padding:0;border:0;background:transparent;color:var(--text,#292b28);caret-color:var(--accent,#b34d2b)}.ds-field input::placeholder{color:var(--muted,#696b64);opacity:1}.ds-field input:focus-visible{outline:none}.ds-field button{font-family:\"DM Sans\",system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;align-self:stretch;padding:0 16px;border:0;border-radius:0 7px 7px 0;background:var(--text,#292b28);color:var(--surface,#fff);cursor:pointer;transition:opacity .15s}.ds-field button:hover{opacity:.8}.ds-field button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#9d4224);outline-offset:4px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Recent city chip",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "chip-city",
      "description": "Current place with a disambiguating qualifier.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-city\" aria-current=\"true\" aria-label=\"Show weather for London, Ontario, Canada, 42.98°, -81.23°\" title=\"London, Ontario, Canada, 42.98°, -81.23°\"><span class=\"ds-city-name\">London</span><span class=\"ds-city-qualifier\"> · Ontario</span></button>",
      "css": ".ds-city{font-family:\"DM Sans\",system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;flex:none;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:36px;max-width:300px;padding:6px 14px;border:0;border-radius:6px;background:transparent;color:var(--text,#292b28);white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;cursor:pointer}.ds-city[aria-current=\"true\"]{background:var(--surface,#fff)}.ds-city-name{max-width:140px;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}.ds-city-qualifier{max-width:130px;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:var(--muted,#696b64);white-space:pre}.ds-city:hover{background:var(--raised,#f1f0ec)}.ds-city:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#9d4224);outline-offset:4px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Weather panel",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "panel",
      "description": "Flat neutral information container.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-panel\"><h2>Weather details</h2><p>Selected day’s conditions</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-panel{font-family:\"DM Sans\",system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;padding:24px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e5e5df);border-radius:16px;background:var(--surface,#fff);color:var(--text,#292b28)}.ds-panel h2{margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.4}.ds-panel p{margin:4px 0 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted,#696b64)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Current conditions",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "current-panel",
      "description": "Accent-wash reading; sample values are illustrative.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-current\"><h2>Current weather</h2><div class=\"ds-temperature\">29<span>°C</span></div><p>Clear sky</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-current{font-family:\"DM Sans\",system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;padding:24px;border-radius:16px;background:var(--accent-soft,#f8ece3);color:var(--accent-ink,#71371f)}.ds-current h2{margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.4}.ds-temperature{margin-top:26px;font-size:88px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.04em;white-space:nowrap}.ds-temperature span{font-size:32px;vertical-align:top;position:relative;top:10px;letter-spacing:-.02em}.ds-current p{margin:8px 0 0;font-size:23px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.02em;line-height:1.3}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Forecast interval",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "forecast-row",
      "description": "Selected day interval; preview data is illustrative.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-forecast\" aria-pressed=\"true\" aria-label=\"Show Monday forecast\"><span>Mon</span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"4\"/><path d=\"M12 2v2M12 20v2M2 12h2M20 12h2m-3.66-5.66 1.41-1.41M4.93 4.93l1.41 1.41m0 11.32-1.41 1.41m12.73-1.41 1.41 1.41\"/></svg><small>0%</small><span class=\"ds-range\"><span>21°</span><span class=\"ds-track\"><span></span></span><span>32°</span></span><svg class=\"ds-chevron\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></button>",
      "css": ".ds-forecast{font-family:\"DM Sans\",system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;display:grid;grid-template-columns:80px 32px 46px 1fr 24px;align-items:center;gap:12px;width:100%;min-height:48px;padding:4px 10px;margin:3px 0;text-align:left;border:0;border-radius:6px;background:transparent;color:var(--text,#292b28);cursor:pointer}.ds-forecast:hover{background:var(--raised,#f1f0ec)}.ds-forecast[aria-pressed=\"true\"]{background:var(--accent-soft,#f8ece3)}.ds-forecast:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#9d4224);outline-offset:4px;}.ds-forecast>span:first-child{font-weight:500}.ds-forecast svg{width:21px;height:21px;fill:none;stroke:var(--accent,#b34d2b);stroke-width:1.65;stroke-linecap:round}.ds-forecast small{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted,#696b64);text-align:right}.ds-range{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px}.ds-range>span:first-child{color:var(--muted,#696b64)}.ds-track{height:5px;min-width:20px;flex:1;position:relative;background:var(--raised,#f1f0ec);border-radius:9px}.ds-track span{position:absolute;left:15%;width:70%;height:5px;background:var(--accent-track,#ebc2aa);border-radius:9px}.ds-forecast[aria-pressed=\"true\"] .ds-track span{background:var(--accent,#b34d2b)}.ds-forecast .ds-chevron{width:16px;height:16px;color:var(--muted,#696b64);stroke:currentColor;justify-self:end}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Metric selector",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "metric-option",
      "description": "Tonal hourly-metric selection.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-metrics\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Hourly metric\"><button aria-pressed=\"true\">Temperature</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">Rain</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">Wind</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-metrics{display:flex;gap:4px}.ds-metrics button{font-family:\"DM Sans\",system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;font-size:13px;min-height:36px;padding:6px 10px;border:0;border-radius:6px;background:transparent;color:var(--muted,#696b64);cursor:pointer}.ds-metrics button[aria-pressed=\"true\"],.ds-metrics button:hover{background:var(--raised,#f1f0ec)}.ds-metrics button[aria-pressed=\"true\"]{color:var(--text,#292b28)}.ds-metrics button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#9d4224);outline-offset:4px;}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Daylight horizon",
    "overview": "A restrained daylight palette pairs warm ivory and white with charcoal readings and burnt-orange data. Flat panels, fine rules and tabular numerals keep the interface quiet while the weather remains prominent. Dark mode preserves the same hierarchy through deep olive surfaces and pale apricot accents.\n\nThe system favors precise, legible information over decorative imagery. A self-hosted variable face, the retained SVG weather icon family and a small authored wind mark establish continuity across controls, readings and charts.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm neutral surfaces with a reserved orange data accent.",
      "Tabular readings and compact, sentence-case labels.",
      "Flat rounded containers with tonal selection.",
      "Keyboard-visible controls and explicit data states."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Data Accent Rule",
        "body": "Use the orange family for weather marks, chart data, selected intervals and a small number of actions; use neutral text for ordinary readings.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Reading Hierarchy Rule",
        "body": "Reserve the largest regular-weight figures for current temperature; keep section headings compact and semibold.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Surface Rule",
        "body": "Separate resting panels with tone and fine borders; reserve the ambient shadow for the floating search results.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use the matching theme palette for surfaces, text, charts and focus.",
      "Do retain tabular numerals, explicit units and local-time context.",
      "Do keep long city names readable through wrapping in headings and scrolling recent-place chips with full accessible names.",
      "Do represent unavailable readings with an em dash and provide honest loading, saved-data and error messages.",
      "Do reuse the existing SVG icon family and authored vector marks."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't replace data marks with emoji or unrelated icon styles.",
      "Don't add shadows to resting weather panels.",
      "Don't use the display temperature size for ordinary details or section titles.",
      "Don't truncate an accessible city name or collapse distinct same-name locations into one ambiguous label."
    ]
  }
}
